[h1]Deep Frontier[/h1]
[b]An industrial frontier expansion for the Iron Teeth.[/b] Dig into the deep ore below your map, pour concrete, smelt steel, run coal, oil and nuclear power, keep your beavers fed and healthy, and push all the way to a rocket launch, while managing radiation, smog and workplace injuries.

[i]Iron Teeth only. Timberborn 1.1.2.8 or later. The mod is playable and actively developed: expect balance changes between versions.[/i]

[h2]What's in it[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]64 new buildings, 55 goods and 75 recipes[/b], built to match Timberborn's own look and placement rules.
[*][b]Deep ore:[/b] Deep Drills and Deep Mines reach finite deposits and permanent veins below the surface; the Deep Ore Processor turns the ore into coal, crude oil, uranium and alloy.
[*][b]Construction materials:[/b] sandstone and limestone quarries and pits, stone crusher, cement kiln and concrete mixer; concrete and masonry blocks, scaffolds, side platforms, overhangs and reinforced dams.
[*][b]Heavy industry:[/b] steel mill, chemical works, precision machine works, electrolysis and cryogenic liquefaction plants, water treatment.
[*][b]Power:[/b] reinforced hydro turbine; coal (5,000 hp) and oil (20,000 hp) power plants that run without workers and burn fuel only while your network needs power; and a nuclear reactor that can melt down if you neglect it.
[*][b]Radiation:[/b] radioactive waste you must refine, store in a vault or export; radioactive water that stops pumps and contaminates goods; and a new [b]Radioactive Tide[/b] weather event. Contamination sensors and supported sluices can measure radiation.
[*][b]Food:[/b] fishery works, fish hatchery, greenhouse (with aquaponics), fertilizer works and food packaging.
[*][b]Civic life:[/b] a restaurant with real table service, where a full meal earns the Fine Dining bonus; a grocery store; a hospital and public health lab; a bathhouse, town plaza and observation deck.
[*][b]Smog:[/b] industry pollutes the air around it; plant trees or build smog scrubbers.
[*][b]Workforce risks:[/b] dangerous jobs can injure beavers; bots need upkeep; a technical school trains specialists.
[*][b]Science and the rocket program:[/b] materials laboratory, archive excavation, rocket assembly hangar, mission control and launch pad, with missions to launch.
[*][b]Building passages:[/b] buildings that touch share their insides, stacked or side by side, so beavers can walk through one building to reach the next.
[/list]

[h2]Required mods[/h2]
Subscribe to these too (Steam lists them under Required items):
[list]
[*]Harmony
[*]Moddable Timberborn
[*]Moddable Tool Groups
[*]Mod Settings (eMka)
[*]TimberUi
[*]Moddable Recipes
[*]New Styles
[*]Pump to Tank
[*]Flywheels
[*]Teleporter Station
[*]Timber Pipes
[*]Solar Panel (northforge)
[*]Expanded Storage
[*]Conveyor Belts
[*]Powered Tubeway
[*]Power Lines
[*]Map Transformer
[/list]
Optional: Moddable Weathers (for the Radioactive Tide weather) and Sluice is Back! (radiation-aware sluices).

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Not compatible with Hooman Stairs.[/b] Deep Frontier links touching buildings itself. While Hooman Stairs is enabled, Deep Frontier turns its building passages off and says so on the main menu.
[*]Works with existing Iron Teeth saves. Deep ore deposits and veins are map objects: place them in the map editor (Deep Frontier adds them there), or play a map that has them.
[/list]

[h2]Feedback[/h2]
Please report bugs in the comments with your game log (Documents\Timberborn\Logs) and, if you can, a save.
